# Copy to .env and fill in what you have. .env is gitignored and optional:
# every variable here has a working default in the Makefile, so a fresh clone
# runs without one. Its purpose is the values that cannot have a default.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   make dev          # Postgres, migrations, then the API

# ── Needed only to sign in from the app for real ─────────────────────────────
# Google issues one client id per platform. Without them the sign-in screen
# reports the provider unavailable rather than failing silently.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_IOS=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_ANDROID=
#
# The server checks a provider token against these. Placeholders are fine until
# a real sign-in happens; `make token` does not involve them at all.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS=
# APPLE_CLIENT_IDS=

# ── Where the app looks for the API ──────────────────────────────────────────
# On a physical device this CANNOT be localhost — use your machine's LAN
# address, or the app will look for the server on the phone itself.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8080

# ── Overrides you are unlikely to need ───────────────────────────────────────
# DB_URL=postgres://binder:binder@localhost:5432/binder?sslmode=disable
# PORT=8080
# SESSION_JWT_SECRET=            # 32 bytes minimum, enforced in code
# CARD_IMAGES_BUCKET_URL=        # file://… locally, gs://… in deployment
